; libm (the Round primitive's floor); prototype type-matches ELObj.scaly's.
function floor(x: double) returns double extern
; ... and the rest of the transcendental family the numeric primitives call
; 1:1 (primitive.cxx Exp/Log/Sin/.../Expt). `modf` is NOT declared: its only
; two uses (Truncate, InexactToExact) want the integer part, which is
; floor/ceil by sign — an out-parameter extern buys nothing here.
function ceil(x: double) returns double extern
function sqrt(x: double) returns double extern
function exp(x: double) returns double extern
function log(x: double) returns double extern
function sin(x: double) returns double extern
function cos(x: double) returns double extern
function tan(x: double) returns double extern
function asin(x: double) returns double extern
function acos(x: double) returns double extern
function atan(x: double) returns double extern
function atan2(y: double, x: double) returns double extern
; same prototype as ELObj.scaly's (extern declares must type-match cross-root)
function pow(x: double, y: double) returns double extern

; The civil-time shim (packages/scaly/0.1.0/scaly/time/ctime.c, built by
; tools/ctime.sh into every libscaly.a and every scalyc link). These three
; are NOT direct libc externs because their libc originals fail both halves
; of the containment rule in CLAUDE.md: they read `struct tm`, a libc STRUCT
; whose field order the single committed seed may not assume across the four
; LP64 targets (a), and they drive sscanf/sprintf, VARIADIC calls a
; fixed-prototype Scaly extern cannot make faithfully on arm64 (b).
; Everything crossing the boundary is 64-bit, so no i32 declaration is needed
; (memory llvm-extern-i32-abi).
function scaly_time_now() returns i64 extern
function scaly_time_format(k: i64, use_gmt: i64, out: pointer[u8]) returns i64 extern
function scaly_time_conv(s: pointer[u32], n: i64) returns i64 extern

; Primitive — the built-in procedures over ELObj (Style/Primitive.cxx). The
; reference has one class per primitive; here each is a prim_id arm of a single
; dispatch. Inc-3 starter set: the pure-ELObj primitives (arithmetic,
; comparison, pairs/lists, predicates, not) — the reference's "install first"
; batch. Strings/chars/vectors and the grove / sosofo / style primitives join
; as their machinery lands. prim_id values are the install order in Interpreter.

